   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,244:               cli.py:  103: PRE_SUBMISSION_REVIEW_2026-04-08.md
    INFO: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,251:         converter.py:   14: PRE_SUBMISSION_REVIEW_2026-04-08.md
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Pre-Submission Referee Report
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,282:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Paper
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,290:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Wage Subsidies vs. Vocational Training for Young Men: Experimental Evidence from a Factorial
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,293:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Randomized Controlled Trial
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,294:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,295:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Authors
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,295:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Anonymous
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Date
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : 2026-04-08
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Review Standard
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,299:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Leading Field Journal
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,300:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Overall Assessment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,320:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The paper uses a 2x2 factorial RCT among 1,347 young men to show that employment vouchers generate a 39.9 pp
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,327:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: short-run employment effect that fades to 3.0 pp by endline, vocational training alone is ineffective, and the two
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,329:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interventions exhibit zero complementarity. The contribution is rated as 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,329:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Incremental
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,399:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : the individual findings
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,461:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (voucher fade-out, null training) replicate well-known patterns, while the factorial interaction test -- the main
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,497:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: value-added -- yields a precisely estimated null in an anonymized context without cost data. The single most critical
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,515:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: issue is the anonymized setting: without disclosing the country, voucher structure, training content, compliance
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,520:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: rates, or timing of surveys relative to the intervention, the paper is an experiment without a denominator, preventing
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,521:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: any meaningful assessment of external validity or mechanisms.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,522:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Preliminary Recommendation
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,523:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Desk reject
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,524:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Contribution 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,525:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,525:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Referee Assessment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,526:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Part 1 -- Central Contribution
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,538:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The paper claims to show, via a factorial RCT among 1,347 young men, that employment vouchers generate large
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,541:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: short-run employment gains that mostly fade out, vocational training alone is ineffective, and the two interventions
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,542:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: exhibit zero complementarity.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,543:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,544:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Is this finding genuinely new?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,598:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Partially. The large short-run voucher effect that fades is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,637:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: well-documented (Galasso et al. 2004; Levinsohn et al. 2014; Groh et al. 2016). The null training
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: result is consistent with the pessimistic end of Card et al. (2018). The genuinely novel contribution
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,667:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: is the factorial test of interaction -- but the finding of zero interaction, while policy-relevant, is a null
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: result on an effect that few priors would place far from zero anyway.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Closest prior paper:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,689:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Groh et al. (2016) evaluate a voucher program for young people in Jordan
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,699:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: with similarly strong short-run effects and fade-out. The factorial design adds the interaction test,
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: but this paper does not offer the institutional or theoretical depth that Groh et al. provide.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,702:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rating:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,704:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Incremental
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The individual findings (voucher fade-out, null training) replicate well-known patterns. The factorial
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,757:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interaction test is the value-added, but a precisely estimated zero on one interaction term in one
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,763:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: anonymous context, without cost data or a structural model, does not clear the bar for a significant
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: advance. The paper confirms rather than challenges prevailing priors.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Part 2 -- Identification and Credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What variation identifies the main result?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Individual-level random assignment in a 2x2 factorial design. This is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,770:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: clean experimental variation.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,771:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Is it plausibly exogenous?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,775:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Yes, the balance table and placebo tests are consistent with successful randomization.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,776:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The design is well-executed on this dimension.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,777:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Main threats:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,778:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Attrition:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  7-10% attrition from baseline to survey waves, which is moderate. Lee bounds are
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,785:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: implemented but midline salary bounds span zero (
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,786:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: -12.19, +45.04
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,795:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ), materially undermining the
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,798:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: headline salary result. The paper emphasizes endline salary bounds (strictly positive) while the
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,799:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: midline salary bounds receive less emphasis.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,800:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,801:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Anonymized context:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,815:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The country, implementing agency, voucher structure, training content,
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,821:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: duration, timing between waves, and voucher amount are all undisclosed. This makes it impossible
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,822:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to assess external validity, compare with other studies, or understand mechanisms.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,823:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,824:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: No compliance data:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,834:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  No discussion of take-up rates. Did all voucher recipients use the voucher?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Did all training assignees attend? Without compliance data, the enormous midline employment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,839:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: effect (39.9 pp) is difficult to interpret.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,841:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Outcome definitions are vague:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,841:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Employment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  and 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,844:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,844:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: salary
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,849:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  are undefined beyond variable names.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,851:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Are these self-reported? Administrative? Is salary inclusive of the subsidy at midline?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,852:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What would a skeptical econometrician say?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,865:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The identification is clean, but the paper is a black box. Without
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,870:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: knowing the country, voucher structure, training duration, compliance rate, or measurement protocol, the numbers
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,871:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: are uninterpretable beyond the narrow point that 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,872:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: this particular voucher in this particular setting had a large
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: short-run effect.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,875:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,876:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  If midline was measured while the voucher was still active, the result is purely mechanical.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,877:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Part 3 -- Analyses: Required and Suggested
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,878:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Required:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,878:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,879:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,880:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,880:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Disclose the context.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The country, implementing organization, voucher
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,911:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: value/duration, training content/duration, and timing of midline/endline relative to intervention must
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,914:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: be revealed. If midline occurs during the voucher period, the employment effect is mechanical and
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the entire framing collapses.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,916:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,916:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,917:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,918:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,918:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Report compliance/take-up rates.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  What fraction of voucher recipients actually used
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the voucher? What fraction of training assignees completed training? Readers need the first stage to
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,928:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interpret magnitudes.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,932:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Clarify outcome measurement.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Are outcomes self-reported or administrative? What
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: does 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: employment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  mean? What currency? Is salary inclusive of the subsidy itself at midline?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,940:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,940:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Address whether midline employment includes subsidized jobs.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,943:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  If the voucher is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,944:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: still active at midline and 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,944:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,945:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: employment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,946:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,948:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  captures the subsidized position, the 39.9 pp effect is not
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,949:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: evidence that vouchers 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,950:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,950:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: increase employment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,951:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,952:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  in any economically meaningful sense.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,953:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,953:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,954:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,955:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,955:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,956:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Provide a pre-analysis plan or registration.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,961:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  No mention of pre-registration or PAP.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,962:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Given the large number of outcomes, the multiple hypothesis testing problem must be addressed.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,963:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Suggested:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,964:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,964:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,965:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,966:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Cost-effectiveness analysis.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The paper repeatedly discusses policy implications but
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: provides no cost data.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,971:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,972:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,972:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,973:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,974:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,975:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Heterogeneous treatment effects.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,977:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Explore whether the voucher effect varies by baseline
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,978:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: characteristics (education, prior work experience).
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,979:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,980:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,983:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Decompose the salary effect into extensive and intensive margins.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,984:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  A
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,986:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: conditional-on-employment analysis would be informative.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,986:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,987:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,988:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,988:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,989:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,990:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Report attrition by arm.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,991:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Differential attrition across arms should be tested directly and
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,992:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reported.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,993:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,994:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,995:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,995:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,996:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,997:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Address multiple hypothesis testing.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:28,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  With 5+ outcomes at 2 time points, some
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,000:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: correction (Bonferroni, Westfall-Young) is necessary.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,001:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Part 4 -- Literature Positioning
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,003:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The literature review is competent but formulaic. The right canonical references are cited.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,004:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Missing references:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,004:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,006:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Alfonsi et al. (2020, QJE) on vocational training vs. firm-based training in Uganda
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,007:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,009:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bassi and Nansamba (2022, AER) on screening and hiring in developing countries
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,010:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,011:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Blattman and Dercon (2018, QJE) on factory employment interventions
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,011:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,012:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: McKenzie (2017, WB Research Observer) on small sample issues in RCTs
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,013:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The paper does not adequately position itself relative to the 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: graduation approach
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,015:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,016:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  literature (Banerjee et al. 2015 is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cited but not substantively engaged).
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,018:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Part 5 -- Journal Fit and Recommendation
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,019:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Best realistic targets:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,028:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  In its current form, not ready for a top-field journal (QJE, AER, Econometrica, ReStud, JPE).
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The anonymized context, missing compliance data, absent cost analysis, and incremental contribution are
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: collectively disqualifying.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,032:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Preliminary recommendation:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,033:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Desk reject
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,034:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What would it take?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,042:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Reveal the context; report compliance data; provide cost-effectiveness analysis; offer a
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,044:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: structural or theoretical framework; show unexpected heterogeneity or a mechanism; ideally include longer-term
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,045:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: follow-up.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,046:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Best alternative outlet:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,047:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Journal of Development Economics, World Bank Economic Review, or Journal of Human
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,048:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Resources.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Part 6 -- Questions to the Authors
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,055:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What country is this study conducted in, and what is the institutional setting? Was the voucher still
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,056:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: active at midline? If so, the headline result is mechanical.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,057:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,058:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What are the take-up and compliance rates for each treatment arm?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,059:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,060:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Does the midline salary measure include the subsidy payment itself, or only the worker
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,060:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,061:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s take-home
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,062:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: wage net of the subsidy?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,063:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,069:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Why is there no multiple testing correction? The endline LFP result (p = 0.008) would likely not
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: survive a Westfall-Young correction across all 10 outcome-period combinations.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,071:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,074:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What is the per-capita cost of each intervention? You make repeated claims about optimal budget
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: allocation without any cost data.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,076:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  6 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,077:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How do you reconcile the strictly positive Lee bounds on endline salary (
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,078:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,079:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: +1.26, +18.94
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,079:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ) with the
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,082:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: insignificant OLS point estimate (6.954, p=0.273)?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  7 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Was this trial pre-registered, and if so, what were the pre-specified primary outcomes?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,085:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. Unsupported Claims 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Identification Integrity
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,088:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Causal Overclaiming (must address)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,090:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,091:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,091:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Abstract: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,101:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,110:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: These results suggest that demand-side wage subsidies generate large
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,112:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: short-run employment effects that substantially fade over time, while supply-side training alone is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,113:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ineffective.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,115:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Ineffective
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,117:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,123:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is a causal claim about the general class of supply-side training
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,124:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: programs, but the paper only tests one specific training program. Fix: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,125:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,126:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: produced no detectable
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,127:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: effects in this setting.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,129:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,130:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,130:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,131:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Section 7.1: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,133:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,137:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: These effects almost certainly reflect the mechanical channel: the
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,139:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: voucher subsidizes employment, and firms respond by hiring participants.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,140:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,145:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- Treats a mechanism as
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,148:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: established fact without firm-level data, take-up data, or direct evidence on firm decision-making.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fix: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,150:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,151:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: are consistent with the mechanical channel.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,151:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,152:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,154:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Section 7.1: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,171:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Individuals who received vouchers are more likely to remain in the labor
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: force even after the subsidized match dissolves, suggesting that the work experience may have
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: shifted their reservation utility, search intensity, or labor market attachment.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,180:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- Proposes three
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: specific behavioral mechanisms without any data on any of them. Should be explicitly labeled as
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: speculative.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CRITICAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Section 7.1: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Together, these findings suggest that vouchers generate lasting changes
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: in labor market engagement.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Lasting
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is doing heavy work with only two time points and a
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: faded employment effect. Should acknowledge limited time horizon.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Section 7.2: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: when the demand-side constraint is relaxed, employment responds
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dramatically
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- Conflates the mechanical subsidy effect with a structural claim about binding
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: constraints.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  6 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Conclusion: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,212:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,213:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: wage subsidies are powerful short-run instruments for increasing youth
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: employment
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,215:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- Generalizes from one voucher in one context to 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,216:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,216:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: wage subsidies
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,217:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,217:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  as a class.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,218:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  7 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,218:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,219:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,219:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,220:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Conclusion: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,220:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the marginal dollar is better spent expanding voucher coverage than adding
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,223:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: a training component
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,224:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,224:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- Requires cost data the paper explicitly acknowledges it lacks.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  8 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,226:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,226:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,227:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,230:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Section 5.1.3: The persistence narrative rests on a single significant LFP coefficient. The
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,231:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: LFP effect could reflect measurement artifact.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Generalization Issues
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,233:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  9 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,233:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,235:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Introduction: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,236:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,237:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: almost no study has experimentally varied both simultaneously to test for
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,238:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interaction effects
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,239:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,240:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- Unverified priority assertion. The claim is vague enough to be unfalsifiable.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,241:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  10 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,241:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,242:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MAJOR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,243:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,243:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Section 2.2: Generalizes from one program to 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,244:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,245:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the class of short-to-medium-duration
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,246:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: vocational training programs.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,247:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-08 09:39:29,247:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  11 
